 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Time Complexity**: Allocation is $O(1)$ for pool lookups [G].
--   **Memory Complexity**: Bounded by pool sizes (e.g., 4 MB + 430 MB) [S1, unofficial].
--   **Performance**: Enables interactive rendering of large volumes (e.g., $2048^3$) on limited hardware (e.g., 512 MB GPU) [S1, unofficial].
--   **Strengths**: Memory efficiency, scalability to large logical volumes.
--   **Limitations**: Requires careful tuning of pool sizes to avoid thrashing or overflow.
-
+-   **Time Complexity**: Pool lookups are $O(1)$ [G].
+-   **Memory Complexity**: Bounded by the fixed pool budgets (e.g., 4 MB + 430 MB) [S1, unofficial].
+-   **Performance**: Enables interactive rendering of large volumes (e.g., $2048^3$) on limited hardware (e.g., NVIDIA 8800 GTS with 512 MB VRAM) [S1, unofficial].
+-   **Strengths**: Memory efficiency, scalability to large logical volumes, and support for on-the-fly GPU brick generation [S1, unofficial].
